`Enable touch input in Editor. ` https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110893/changes/e267e5488e11e1b1369e9bf7413b61ff4e3ada74

I tested the last commit on an Android Samsung tablet and didn't notice any regressions (as long as touch input was used), and there were hardly any functions/buttons that could benefit from multitouch.

This time I connected a Bluetooth mouse to my tablet and tested the mouse input. The buttons do not react to mouse clicks, neither in the editor nor in the game window (export template).

@Kazox61 It is possible to force this behavior (tested macOS Godot Editor) if you have no testing options with a BT mouse + Android.

```cpp
	bool touchscreen_available = true; //DisplayServer::get_singleton()->is_touchscreen_available();
	if (touchscreen_available) {
```
